# tina4-nodejs — Cursor Rules

Tina4 Node.js/TypeScript v3.10.70. 54 built-in features, zero dependencies. Node.js 20+. ESM only.

## Key Patterns

```typescript
// File-based routing: src/routes/api/users/get.ts → GET /api/users
import type { Tina4Request, Tina4Response } from "@tina4/core";

export default async function (req: Tina4Request, res: Tina4Response) {
  return res.json({ users: [] });
}

// Or explicit registration
import { Router } from "@tina4/core";
Router.get("/api/users", async (req, res) => res.json({ users: [] }));
```

## Critical Rules

- ESM only — use .js extensions in imports even for .ts files
- No Express/Fastify — native node:http
- No decorators — convention-based models with static properties
- Route params: `{id}` in URLs, `[id]` in directory names
- Auth: POST/PUT/DELETE require auth. Use `/** @noauth */` JSDoc to make public
- GET is public. Use `/** @secure */` JSDoc to protect
- Queue job payload: `job.payload` not `job.data`
- Import from "@tina4/core", "@tina4/orm" — not internal paths
- Default port: 7148
- Entry point: `import { startServer } from "@tina4/core"; startServer({ port, host });`

## Project Structure

Routes in `src/routes/`, models in `src/models/`, templates in `src/templates/`, static in `public/`.

See llms.txt for complete API reference.
